import LOEIS.A387.A387386.Defs

set_option linter.unusedVariables false

/-!
# A387386

Array read by antidiagonals, where the n-th row lists primes p such that p, p+x_1, ..., p+x_1+...+x_k are consecutive primes, where (x_1, ..., x_k) is the n-th composition corresponding to an admissible prime tuple pattern (see A387383).

The 66 terms known to OEIS, indexed from `1`.

Skeleton generated by `lake exe oeis-gen`; every declaration is a `sorry` placeholder.
-/

namespace A387386

/-- Known terms of `flat`, starting at index `1`. -/
def flatData : List flatRetType :=
  [2, 3, 3, 5, 5, 7, 7, 11, 13, 23,
    11, 17, 19, 31, 7, 13, 29, 37, 47, 13,
    5, 17, 41, 43, 53, 37, 11, 89, 19, 59,
